# Parker Luck {2}{B}: "two target players" is one instance of the word "target", so the same player can't be chosen twice
# (CR 115.3, 601.2c). Bot1 can't name Bot2 for both, and one player is not two; it must choose Bot1 and Bot2. Bot1 reveals Sol Ring
# (mana value 1) and Bot2 reveals Serra Angel (5): Bot1 loses 5 and Bot2 loses 1, not 10 from revealing Serra Angel twice.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Parker Luck
Swamp x5
Sol Ring
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x7
Serra Angel
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Parker Luck.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T1 Bot1.End]
! Bot1.Target(Bot2; Bot2)
! Bot1.Target(Count: 1)
Bot1.Target(Bot1; Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 15
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot2.Revealed = Serra Angel
